Subject: Re: spatio-temporal random effects vs colonisation & extinction probabilities

Hi Charles,

If you are interested explicitly understanding an interaction, then I would suggest using something like the Rota et al. model instead of the multi-species models in spOccupancy. The models in spOccupancy account for residual species correlations, but they are not explicitly designed to quantify species co-occurrence patterns like the Rota model. While such estimates could be derived from the models in spOccupancy, it would be a good amount of work and would involve a very nuanced interpretation. Altogether, I think going with something like the Rota model is probably a better bet for your objectives.

Cheers,

Jeff

